## Problem

The Flask app `/search` page was throwing a JavaScript error:
```
TypeError: window.rangesLoader.populateSelectWithFallback is not a function
```

This prevented the "Part of Speech" dropdown from being populated with grammatical information options.

## Root Cause

The `search.html` template was calling `window.rangesLoader.populateSelectWithFallback()`, but the loaded script `ranges-loader.js` didn't have this method. The method existed only in `ranges-loader-debug.js`, indicating an outdated script issue.

## Solution

Added the missing methods to `ranges-loader.js`:

1. **`populateSelectWithFallback()`** - Main method that tries to populate from API first, then falls back to hardcoded values
2. **`getFallbackValues()`** - Helper method that provides fallback data for different range types  
3. **Improved jQuery safety check** - Prevents "$ is not defined" errors when Select2 library isn't available

The implementation reuses the existing fallback data structure already present in the script, ensuring consistency.

## Testing

Verified the fix works correctly:
- ✓ `populateSelectWithFallback` method exists and is callable
- ✓ Method successfully populates dropdown with fallback values when API is unavailable
- ✓ Select populated with 9 grammatical options (Any, Noun, Verb, Adjective, etc.)
- ✓ No JavaScript errors in console

## Changes Made

```javascript
// Added to ranges-loader.js
getFallbackValues(rangeId) {
    // Convert existing fallback data to expected format
    if (this.fallbackData[rangeId] && this.fallbackData[rangeId].values) {
        return this.fallbackData[rangeId].values.map(item => ({
            id: item.value,
            value: item.value,
            abbrev: item.text !== item.value ? item.text : null
        }));
    }
    return [];
}

async populateSelectWithFallback(selectElement, rangeId, options = {}) {
    // Try API first, fall back to hardcoded values if needed
    const success = await this.populateSelect(selectElement, rangeId, options);
    if (!success) {
        // Populate with fallback values
        const fallbackValues = this.getFallbackValues(rangeId);
        // ... populate select element ...
    }
    return true;
}
```

